FILE: drift.rs
MOD: commands/drift
OWNS: dependency drift detection — actual imports vs declared depends_on; stale-declared reverse drift
PROFILE: [io, pure-core]
CHANGE-FREQUENCY: volatile

DriftItem: record [pub] — module_id, file, import_raw, line_number, target_module, kind ("forbidden"|"undeclared")
StaleDeclaredItem: record [pub, Serialize] — module_id, file, declared_dep
DriftResult: record [pub] — items: Vec<DriftItem>, scanned_count: usize, stale_declared: Vec<StaleDeclaredItem>

check: &ArchContext → Result<DriftResult, String> [io]
  calls: ctx::build_index, imports::extract_imports, resolve::is_external_import, check_drift
  called-by: run, stale::run
  note: stale_declared field is always empty Vec — stale computation runs in run() only

run: bool * bool → Result<(), String> [io, boundary]
  calls: ArchContext::load, check, check_stale_declared (if flag set), report_drift

check_stale_declared: &ArchContext → Vec<StaleDeclaredItem> [io]
  note: build_dep_graph(resolve_self=true) to include same-container refs; computes declared − actual

check_drift: &HashSet<String> * &str * &str * &HashSet<String> * &HashSet<String> * &HashSet<String> * &Module * &str * &Import * &mut Vec<DriftItem> → ()
  note: groups resolved targets by container; broad fan-out (>1 target per container) collapses to [broad match] violation

report_drift: bool * bool * usize * &[DriftItem] * &[StaleDeclaredItem] → Result<(), String>
  note: exit code 1 only on forbidden violations; undeclared and stale-declared exit 0

DEPENDS-ON: context, imports, resolve, depgraph

KEY-INVARIANTS:
- broad-match declared check uses d.starts_with(&format!("{}/", target_container)) — direction matters; reversing it (v0.5.2 bug) suppresses all broad-match warnings for declared cross-container deps
- forbidden deps exit code 1; undeclared-only is a warning (exit 0) — stale inherits this behaviour via DriftResult
- stale_declared computation only runs when --stale-declared flag is passed; check() signature is unchanged (stale.rs unaffected)

